// A module owning neither side may not write the implementation. Nobody else
// has a claim: the trait's module and the type's module each have a reason to
// be the one that decides, and a third has only an opinion about two things it
// does not own.
//
// This is also what makes coherence key equality rather than a search. Two
// implementations conflict only when the trait and the head both match, which
// this rule already makes impossible across modules.
import account
import measure

use account.Account
use measure.Measure

impl Measure for Account {
    fn of(x: Self) -> UInt8 {
        x.balance
    }
}

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    0
}
